{"requirements":[{"id":"firewall-policy","requirement":"Enable a persistent host firewall on node1 that permits SSH and TCP/8080 while rejecting unrelated inbound connections.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Firewalld is active and enabled. Its runtime and permanent public zone retain only SSH and TCP/8080 with target REJECT. Isolated ingress tests directly showed TCP/22 and TCP/8080 accepted and TCP/8081 rejected, both before and after a verified reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-804cd1892eea443a","cmd-d350f9bd9be14d36","cmd-6b54340664d643cb","cmd-ff02a8a303c34053","cmd-f04ecbdceb8e4e65","cmd-a58e3586e10d44bd","cmd-97510a18f9004605","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"platform-preservation","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 were unchanged from baseline through the post-restart state. The implementation used the already-installed RHEL firewalld/nftables stack, and final package health remained sound.","evidence_ids":["cmd-70c8ee5a7ac64031","cmd-e7c21aaf12a3473f","cmd-a58e3586e10d44bd","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":1.0,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The permanent firewall edits directly implemented the requested policy. The temporary namespaces, interfaces, listeners, firewall-interface bindings, and logs used for bounded behavioral testing were necessary evidence and were explicitly removed. The reboot served the mandatory restart protocol and persistence verification. Final lifecycle observations show no failed services, no extra listeners or test files, and healthy package state; boot-related systemd-private directory changes are expected. Restart evidence is complete and independently corroborated: healthy pre-state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered services and policy, and repeated post-restart behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-804cd1892eea443a","cmd-d350f9bd9be14d36","cmd-ff02a8a303c34053","cmd-97510a18f9004605","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied with direct configuration, behavioral, persistence, platform-preservation, and restart-recovery evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol was completed coherently, and no executor-caused residue or unjustified mutations were observed.","limitations":[]}
